e":"ait","d":"2018-10-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"On the project side and I'm sure we'll get into price margin, I feel like we are doing a very effective job of dealing with 232 tariffs understanding 301 and the varied list from list one, list two to list three and potentially list four in taking those increases on -- into point-of-sale prices.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/31/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2018-10-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"…think would be coming through our sales, probably more in the 2% to 3% on the sales impact range, I would say, right now, I could see that increasing as we move on and into '19 into the 3% to 4% range and perhaps a little bit higher depending on how some of these 301 tariffs continue to play out.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/31/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2018-10-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Steve Barger","x":"So you think customers understand that these price increases are coming in and in general are not fighting this necessarily more as you would expect?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/31/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2019-01-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil Schrimsher","x":"…standpoint, but if I set aside LIFO, business performance, teams' performance and seeing inflation come, in our handling of tariffs whether it be the 232, which we really processed on steel and aluminum and the various list of the 301 tariffs, I think we're doing a very good job of matching.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/24/applied-industrial-technologies-ait-q2-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2019-01-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil Schrimsher","x":"I'm a fundamental believer, especially on the tariff side of it.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/24/applied-industrial-technologies-ait-q2-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2019-01-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dave Wells","x":"We expect margins to normalize in Q3 as we passed on the recent supplier price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/24/applied-industrial-technologies-ait-q2-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2019-01-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dave Wells","x":"Adam, we view the price realization -- here again, you were tracking that very discreetly for our same SKU sales year over year, particularly in our service center network.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/24/applied-industrial-technologies-ait-q2-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"A lot of that in advance of some of the rapid increases -- inflationary increases we saw driven by tariffs, you know, for the most part.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"…you know, continued improvement on the large account activity with some beginning of the year price increases that went through, I call it two to three across, you know, that piece of the business, which we think, you know, generally translates to more broadly across the business, but don't…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"Certainly does indicate some of that traction in terms of price realization, but also, you know, the continued benefit of some of the expansionary products and other mix benefit that we see there.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"As referenced in our news release our reported results were impacted by a non-cash intangible impairment charge and related restructuring cost in our Canadian upstream oil and gas operations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"…operating cost, on a reported basis selling, distribution and administrative expenses were, up 3.5%, but down 1.5% year-over-year, when adjusting out the impact of acquisitions, as well as non-recurring restructuring charges in the quarter, which drove nearly one point of the reported increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2019-04-26","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Uhlman","x":"Okay, and then for the guidance, it seems that you might have raised the outlook on organic growth, I think previously you're saying maybe 2% to 3% for the year and now 3% to 4%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2019-08-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"And -- while, there's positive elements in this cycle, there's still uncertainty right though it's the trade or tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/14/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2019-08-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"I'd add just generically that, some -- not some not all of our supply rebate programs for the coming year are cognizant of the fact that we did put some excess inventory on the shelf in our fiscal 2019, both in advance of tariffs and to protect customers from some supply constraints.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/14/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2019-08-14","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Uhlman","x":"Could you tell us what the estimated price realization was for and what you're expecting for this year?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/14/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2019 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2019-08-14","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Dankert","x":"So it really is more just, kind of, flexing the Applied DNA and really, doing which typically we do to get cost out, rather some kind of explicit expense reduction program?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/14/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2019-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2019-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Uhlman","x":"And then, I was wondering, if you could tell us what price realization was this quarter and how you're thinking about that to the rest of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2019-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"On a reported basis, selling, distribution and administrative expenses were up 2.6% year-over-year, but down 2.4% on an organic per day basis, when adjusting out the impact of acquisitions, foreign currency, and non-routine severance expenses in the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2019-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"Reported EPS for the quarter was $1 per share, inclusive of approximately $0.02 of non-routine severance expense, resulting from the previously mentioned cost actions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2019-10-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"As noted in our press release, we are reaffirming our guidance for fiscal 2020, including a sales range of down 2% to up 2%, or down 5% to down 1% on an organic per day basis, as well as earnings per share in the range of $4.20 to $4.50 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2020-01-23","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Michael McGinn","x":"…to up 10 bps still sounds relatively positive and you've never been the primary indicator for the trade war, given you're limited direct exposure to China, but can you comment on how sticky this current run rate is, if we see a broader tariff roll back in subsequent conversations with customers…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/23/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2020-01-23","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Michael McGinn","x":"…still sounds relatively positive and you've never been the primary indicator for the trade war, given you're limited direct exposure to China, but can you comment on how sticky this current run rate is, if we see a broader tariff roll back in subsequent conversations with customers on pricing?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/23/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2020-01-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"If I look at suppliers today, there is still incoming price increases, they moderated from the past, but there will still be some of those coming through and we will be taking them to the marketplace.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/23/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"These costs include severance and facility exit costs in our service center segment, reflecting additional cost actions implemented in response to the weaker demand environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"In addition, personnel spend is being rationalized with staffing alignment to near-term demand, including reductions in force, freezing of new hires, implementation of furloughs and pay reductions and temporary suspension of the company's 401(k) match.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2020-ea.aspx"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2020-08-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"These costs include severance and facility exit cost related to actions implemented in response to the weaker demand environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/12/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2020-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2020 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2020-08-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Uhlman","x":"I wanted to -- I might have missed it, but could you size the magnitude of the temporary cost savings here, this past quarter?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/12/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2020-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2020-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"In addition, we are starting to see a slightly greater level of supplier price increase announcements, which, combined with firming demand, could provide some positive momentum for pricing contribution and margin expansion into the second half of our fiscal year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/28/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2021-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"We do see increased frequency of price increases coming, many of them may have announced periods to allow an orderly implementation to go on in that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2021-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Uhlman","x":"I'm sure the supplier price increases are starting to come through, any opportunity to buy ahead of that?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"Unusual items in the quarter include a $49.5 million pre-tax non-cash impairment charge on certain fixed, leased and intangible assets, as well as non-routine costs of $7.8 million pre-tax related to an inventory reserve charge, facility consolidations and severance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"These business alignment actions are consistent with our internal initiatives and strategic focus going forward and will drive additional cost savings in the back half of our fiscal year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q2-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"We are seeing greater number of suppliers announced price increases in recent months.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"To date, supplier price increases aligned with our broader early cycle expectations, though the backdrop remains fluid as suppliers deal with higher raw material and supply chain costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q3-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2021-08-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"So, while we would -- as you look, it seems to you both cost increases and price increases, you'd be able to enact, you'd see a much larger number.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/17/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2021 Q4","e":"ait","d":"2021-08-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"As you think about that relative mix of the business and those repeat SKUs where we use that as the gauge, as we talk about price that does water down the impact of net yields that 80 to 100 basis points of price realization in the most recent quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/17/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q4-2021-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2022 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2021-10-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"We saw ongoing supplier price increases develop during the quarter, with indications of additional increases in coming quarters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/27/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2022-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2022 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2021-10-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"As a reminder, this assumption only reflects measurable topline contribution from price increases on SKUs sold in both periods, year-over-year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/27/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2022-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2022 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2021-10-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"David K. Wells","x":"And so, today, we think it's appropriate to maintain guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/27/applied-industrial-technologies-inc-ait-q1-2022-ea/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2025-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David Wells","x":"This is up from approximately 100 basis points in the fourth quarter and primarily reflects the effect of pass-through of incremental announced supplier price increases in recent periods as previously discussed.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/28/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2025-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil Schrimsher","x":"But I think there are some manufacturers, a few moved and I think some others are just contemplating looking at the country of origin and when that what the impact will be and when that will come through as a price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/28/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2025-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Dankert","x":"I guess, just as a follow-up, thinking about the Hydrodine synergies, anything you can give us there in terms of is that still on track from both a cross-selling and a cost reduction?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/28/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q1","e":"ait","d":"2025-10-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"David Wells","x":"And reiterate the outlook provided in mid-August.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/28/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2026-01-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil Schrimsher","x":"But hey, that's our view now perhaps the tariff environment is gonna stay moderated at its current level right now as we look out over the rest of the fiscal year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/27/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2026-01-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David Wells","x":"This is up from approximately 200 basis points in the first quarter and primarily reflects the effective pass-through of incrementals now supplier price increases in recent periods.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/27/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q2","e":"ait","d":"2026-01-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David Wells","x":"While the LIFO expense increased partially reflects broader cost inflation, and supplier price increases, we also prudently increased our level of inventory investment in the quarter based on our outlook and firming demand developing across the business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/27/applied-industrial-ait-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2026-04-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"This includes an ongoing dynamic trade policy and tariff backdrop.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/28/ait-q3-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AIT 2026 Q3","e":"ait","d":"2026-04-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil A. Schrimsher","x":"To date, we have not seen a significant impact from recent 